# P3a (docs/tp4-p2p-restore.md section 8): the peer-to-peer KV restore on the cards, standalone (scripts/ci/tp4_p2p_probe.py).
# The cache drive's identity (model and serial through /dev/disk/by-id) and R1's two readings (controller state, namespace size) are checked and printed before the first byte is written; anything
# but `live` refuses. Then one card first (the widest link), every published card, the known object read from the drive into the cards' staging buffers, checked against the host's checksums,
# copied into scratch KV caches and compared byte for byte; a negative arm (one flipped byte on the drive: refused, nothing written, passes when put back); the windows and the p2pmem pools released.
# READ: the last 'P3A verdict=PASS' line (read_gbps, restore_gbps, check_ms_per_chunk, write_ms_per_chunk). NOT-MEASURED (exit 2) is a refusal or a setup failure with nothing written; FAIL is a result.
# WHICH drive and WHICH cards: not here. The runner holds a private file (P2P_ENV_FILE, default ~/.config/qwen-p2p/p3a.env, owned by the runner user, not group- or world-writable) of
# KEY=VALUE lines: P2P_DRIVE_BY_ID (the /dev/disk/by-id/nvme-... path), P2P_DRIVE_MODEL, P2P_DRIVE_SERIAL, P2P_CARDS (comma-separated PCI addresses of the cards whose p2pmem is published).
# Nothing of them reaches a log, a report or this repository (the report carries an 8-hex fingerprint of model and serial).
# NEEDS: the patched tt-kmd loaded for the cards in P2P_CARDS (p2pmem/available == size), the cache drive live (R1) and Opal-unlocked, the cards idle (no serving container: the step refuses one), and
# an image that carries the device-op extension (ttnn.qwen_p2p_staging_alloc / _info, qwen_staging_checksum, qwen_write_blocks_from_staging with row_stride) beside the raw block ops. The probe itself
# runs from the checkout the step mounts at /c2, so it needs the image, not a build of this commit. A reset is the next job's first action (the window is a card window).
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env, to be copied over it on a throwaway commit of the window branch; C2_IMAGE_TAG is the image the orchestrator built with the device-op graft.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=p2p
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-p2p-1
